# test/escape/ROUTES -- every way a region-bound value can reach something that
# outlives its block, enumerated, with what each entry point actually answers.
#
# WHAT THIS IS. The claim this language makes is "no GC, and the compiler will
# not let a value outlive the arena it was allocated in". That claim is only
# worth what its enumeration is worth. Q-053 was found by writing one program;
# two more holes were found by writing this table, because a table has to have
# every row filled in and a bug report does not.
#
# WHY IT HAS TWO AXES. The routes are the obvious axis. The second one is the
# ENTRY POINT, and it is where Q-053's fix turned out to be partial: the check
# fires on the compiling path and not under the interpreter or `mere -t`. That
# is defensible -- the interpreter has no arenas, so nothing dangles there --
# but it means one program gets two answers from one toolchain, so it is
# recorded as a divergence rather than left to be discovered again.
#
# HOW TO READ A ROW.
#   kind       GATED  the check rejects it, and it must keep rejecting it
#              HOLE   accepted today and it DANGLES -- see `q`
#              SAFE   accepted, and safe for a reason stated in the program
#   compiled   what -c / -ll / -w / -rv answer (they must agree; the gate
#              checks that they do, because two backends disagreeing with
#              nothing watching is the failure mode that produced Q-053)
#   interp     what `mere <file>` and `mere -t <file>` answer
#   unreadable backends that refuse this program for a reason that is NOT
#              about escape (a documented codegen subset limit). Their answer
#              is not a verdict and the gate does not read it as one.
#
# A HOLE ROW IS A QUESTION THAT KEEPS BEING ASKED. If one starts being
# rejected, this gate FAILS rather than passing quietly -- a fixed hole has to
# be moved to GATED by hand, because a table that silently agrees with whatever
# the compiler currently does is not checking anything.
#
# route              kind   compiled  interp      unreadable  q
result_container     GATED  REJECT    REJECT      -           -
vec_into_map         GATED  REJECT    ACCEPT      -           Q-053
vec_into_vec         GATED  REJECT    ACCEPT      -           Q-053
map_into_map         GATED  REJECT    ACCEPT      -           Q-053
strbuf_into_vec      GATED  REJECT    ACCEPT      -           Q-053
tuple_into_vec       GATED  REJECT    ACCEPT      -           Q-053
via_fn_arg           GATED  REJECT    REJECT      -           Q-053
loop_store_outer     GATED  REJECT    ACCEPT      -           Q-053
record_field         HOLE   ACCEPT    UNREADABLE  w           Q-067
variant_payload      HOLE   ACCEPT    ACCEPT      w           Q-067
str_out              SAFE   ACCEPT    ACCEPT      w           -
closure_out          SAFE   ACCEPT    ACCEPT      w,rv        -
scalar_out           SAFE   ACCEPT    ACCEPT      -           -
fn_over_carry        SAFE   ACCEPT    ACCEPT      ll,w,rv     -
